// EXPECT: E0239 — `[]` applied to something that is not an array (ADR-0044 §2)
// `[]` makes a view over a `[N]T`. Applied to a scalar there is nothing to view, and the
// operator is refused rather than given a meaning — a one-element view of an `s64` would be a
// different feature with its own design questions.
main :: () {
    n := 7;
    xs := n[];
}
